Description: pvr: VK_EXT_primitives_generated_query from the stream-out counters
 Count generated primitives with an extra STM instruction at the end of the
 stream-out PDS program, which the TA runs once per primitive
 (pvr_rogue_pds_defs.h). The STM has EOP set and writes one dword per
 primitive into a small buffer of the command buffer. Its limit does not
 stop the write on the BXM-4-64 and the STM advances its
 address by one dword per primitive, so a copy of the initial SRC0 is kept in
 a persistent temp and restored before every counting STM: every primitive
 writes the same dword at the start of the buffer. On the BXM-4-64 the low
 word of the STM counter persistent temp (SRC1 bits 31..0) counts every such
 primitive, the high
 word stays unchanged, with or without overflow. The low word is therefore
 read.
 .
 The counter uses its own persistent temps behind the twelve of transform
 feedback (ptemp64 24, 26, 28, and 30 for the copy of SRC0; 32 dwords,
 lls.xml PDS_PERSISTENT_TEMPS_BUFFER_SIZE). A value set in a geometry-only kick
 outside a render pass did not reach the next render (GL through zink, which
 begins and ends the query outside the render pass, read 0 even with a
 preloaded counter), so the temps are only trusted within one graphics sub
 command: begin clears the result and availability in memory, the first draw
 of each graphics sub command while the query is active sets up the temps,
 the end of that sub command adds the counter to the result in memory, and
 the end of the query adds the open sub command, if any, and writes the
 availability. While the query is active the stream-out program ends with the
 counting STM: the transform feedback program while transform feedback is
 active, otherwise a program with only this STM, with stream 0 output to
 memory enabled. Pausing transform feedback does not affect the count.
 Results are one 32-bit report (transform_feedback_query_bits = 32) through
 the existing copy, reset and host paths.
 .
 Rasterizer discard only disables the ISP, the stream-out program in the TA
 still runs, so primitivesGeneratedQueryWithRasterizerDiscard is set. Non-zero
 streams are not supported (maxTransformFeedbackStreams = 1).
 .
 With multiview, a query uses N consecutive indices, N being the number of
 views, and the control stream of a graphics sub command is submitted once
 per view (pvr_process_graphics_cmd()). When the query begins in a graphics
 sub command with more than one view, the render is ended (store), results
 and availability of all N indices are cleared with the query reset program,
 and the render continues (load), as for an occlusion pool change. The clear
 thus runs once, outside the per-view control stream, and each view adds its
 count to the first index. At the end of the query the availability of all N
 indices is written after the sub command, through the deferred timestamp
 path without a timestamp, as for occlusion (0090) and timestamp queries.
 The other indices read zero.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
